    "title": {
     "en": "Sharing a paratha"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Shabnam and Mukta share a chocolate and a paratha. Shabnam folds the paratha over itself so both pieces are exactly equal."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "half",
     "quarter",
     "whole",
     "equal parts"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Shabnam and Mukta want to share their lunch fairly.\nSharing fairly means the parts are equal. If one part is bigger it is not fair.\nTo check, fold the paratha over itself. If the two parts match exactly, they are equal.\nWhen 1 whole is shared equally between 2 people, each share is called a half.\nTwo halves make one whole.\nIf a whole is cut into 4 equal parts, each part is a quarter. Four quarters make a whole.\nCheck chikki: if some is eaten from 3 sides, less than half may be left. Compare with half to decide."
    }
